;; Allocation counters and limits (GHC.Conc's setAllocationCounter, enableAllocationLimit; rts/Schedule.c's
;; schedulePostRunThread, rts/PrimOps.cmm's stg_{get,set}ThreadAllocationCounterzh): each thread's counter counts down
;; the bytes it allocates; when it is below zero with the limit enabled, AllocationLimitExceeded is thrown to the thread
;; as throwToSelf throws it (queued while the thread is masked) and the counter set to the grace, +RTS -xq (100k by
;; default, in 4 KiB blocks). hsi's bytes are the heap objects' words as GHC lays them out (a constructor's and a
;; function's header and fields, a thunk's two header words and free variables), its check every 256 steps where GHC
;; checks at each nursery block: the counts approximate GHC's, the semantics are its.


